==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|pt|roa-opt|temer}}, from {{inh|pt|la|timēre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|timeō||I fear}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|Brazil}} {{IPA|/te.ˈme(ʁ)/|lang=pt}}
** {{a|Paulista}} {{IPA|[te.ˈme(ɹ)]|[-(ɾ)]|lang=pt}}
** {{a|South Brazil}} {{IPA|[te.ˈme(ɻ)]|[-(ɾ)]|lang=pt}}
* {{a|PT}} {{IPA|/tɨ.ˈmeɾ/|lang=pt}}
* {{hyphenation|te|mer|lang=pt}}

===Verb===
{{pt-verb|tem|er}}

# {{lb|pt|intransitive|transitive}} to {{l|en|fear}} {{gloss|to feel fear about something}}
#: {{ux|pt|Não '''tema'''!|Don’t '''be afraid'''!|inline=1}}
#: {{ux|pt|Eu '''temo''' o dia em que ninguém more mais aqui.|I '''fear''' the day no one lives here any more.}}
#: {{syn|pt|[[ter]] [[medo]] ([[de]])}}
#: {{ant|pt|destemer}}
# {{indtr|pt|a|.chiefly|.religion}} to {{l|en|fear}} {{gloss|to feel awe towards}}
#: {{ux|pt|Todo bom cristão '''teme''' a Deus.|Every good Christian '''fears''' God.}}
# {{lb|pt|subordinating}} to be {{l|en|afraid}} {{gloss|''used to express sympathy''}}
#: {{ux|pt|'''Temo''' que não posso ajudar.|'''I’m afraid''' I can’t help.|inline=1}}
# {{indtr|pt|por}} to {{l|en|fear}} for; to {{l|en|worry}} about {{gloss|to be concerned about}}
#: {{ux|pt|Os médicos '''temem''' pela saúde do meu coração.|The doctors '''fear''' for the health of my heart.}}
#: {{syn|pt|[[preocupar]]-[[se]] [[com]]}}

